  "setup": "Requires one Intel Arc Pro B70 32 GB, 63 GB of free host RAM and 85.14 GB for the weights on a local NVMe SSD. Measured on omarchy (EPYC 7443P, 8-channel DDR4, PCIe 4.0 x16, md RAID0 of 4x Samsung 9100 PRO, xfs): system-wide MemAvailable drop 62.2 GB at peak (kit memwatch) - the routed experts (46.7 GB) live in USM host memory, which the xe driver does not charge to the container cgroup (cgroup peak ~11 GB), so the RAM need is the MemAvailable drop, not the container limit. The n-gram (engram) table (32.6 GB) is read from NVMe with O_DIRECT through a 1 GB RAM row cache; no expert NVMe tier (EXL3_NVTIER=0), outputs exact. NEXTN MTP 3 steps / 4 draft tokens (accept length ~2.1-2.5). Context 262,144 tokens with a 270,336-token fp8 KV cache. Vision (images). Kit protocol (local-ai-recipe-kit sweep): prefill 8k 1,141 / 16k 1,152 / 32k 1,145 / 64k 1,134 tok/s; decode C1 41.0, C2 42.3, C3 41.9, C4 41.7 tok/s aggregate, C1 at 32k 43.9; reference panel top-1 0.9883, KL 0.00117.",
